{"id":"01M1TZDC9T74MQ2JYVCTK3X622","ts":"2026-09-06T09:04:56.634Z","task":"TL-289","field":"__decision__","from":"","to":"A profile adapter is one executable, not a shell command. Its provider-specific flags and API calls belong in that user-owned wrapper; branchling passes the profile name, prompt, model and effort through stable environment variables while preserving the existing task-and-retry stdin. Run selects it with --profile and --profile-for <role>=<name>, leaving raw --agent paths unchanged.","actor":"agent:codex","source":"decide","reason":"A profile adapter is one executable, not a shell command. Its provider-specific flags and API calls belong in that user-owned wrapper; branchling passes the profile name, prompt, model and effort through stable environment variables while preserving the existing task-and-retry stdin. Run selects it with --profile and --profile-for <role>=<name>, leaving raw --agent paths unchanged.","session":"tree-526f61f2043f"}
